[{:seon.task/name "image-registration-is-opt-in"
  :seon.task/plan "Done (worktree session reuse, 2026-10-23; Jolt jolt/image-fn-forms-opt-in 686aff7d, eba8826a). Jolt registers every fn literal's source for its state image: fnsrc-flush renders the source, reads it back to check it (fnsrc-row-src), emits image-register-fn-form! per literal and wraps the literal in a maker. Seon writes no image. Now an explicit Jolt compile option, not a changed default: *compiler-options* {:image-fn-forms false} makes a top-level form collect no registrations (backend_scheme.clj fnsrc-regs answers nil), its literals emitted as plain closures with their names; absent or true, Jolt is unchanged for every other user. Jolt reads JOLT_COMPILER_OPTIONS (an EDN map) into *compiler-options*' root at start (post-prelude.ss), as JVM Clojure reads the clojure.compiler.* properties, and Seon sets it in bin/env, so its build, the test runner, root and the agents it forks all compile without registration. Measured: a realistic defn with four literals 5.14 -> 3.47 MB (-33%); a defn of n literals ~1.24 MB and ~172k ticks a literal registering, ~478 KB and ~52k not (-62%, -68%). Known: JOLT_COMPILER_OPTIONS is no input of a test's reach digest (bin/env fixes it), and Jolt's AOT cache keys a namespace without it, so a unit compiled with registration may be loaded without it and the reverse (harmless to Seon, which writes no image)."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.program-cost-test/a-defn-compiles-within-its-estimate}}
 {:seon.task/name "the-emitter-builds-one-buffer"
  :seon.task/plan "Jolt's emitter builds Scheme by nested str concatenation, quadratic in nesting depth (6.2 MB at depth 50, 18 at 100, 59 at 200, 209 at 400) and ~1.4 KB of allocation per output character. Correct: the output is built in one buffer (or s-expressions are handed to Chez). Agents run release or trace-off (source mode with trace doubles every eval).

Measured by worktree session reuse, 2026-10-23 (Jolt eba8826a, image registration off): on 400 real src/seon forms, jolt.backend-scheme/emit-top-form allocated 1,159 MB against the analyzer's 57 MB and the passes' 24 MB: ~2.9 MB a form for ~8 KB of Scheme out, 358 B per output character. Synthetic (fn* [x] (inc (inc ... x))): emit 0.52 MB at depth 50, 1.26 at 100, 3.53 at 200, 11.2 at 400. Cause: every emit fn returns a string and each parent's (str \"(\" a \" \" b \")\") copies its children again, so a character is copied about depth times (Chez strings are 4 B a character). The emitter, not the analyzer, is most of what a compile costs.

Root's go (2026-10-23), option A, kept by this session, in milestones, each a pushed Jolt commit with the gates green (Jolt branch jolt/emitter-one-buffer, on jolt/image-fn-forms-opt-in eba8826a):
(1) the part-tree type (an emit fn answers a tree of parts, not a string) and the one linear writer at emit-top-form (one string port), plus the 8 sites that inspect a child's text realizing it there; the hottest emit fns converted first; then emit allocation measured again on the 400 forms. If it shows no real drop: stop and report before (2).
(2) the rest of the ~406 str sites in the emitter's 157 fns (backend_scheme.clj, 4,505 lines), mechanically.
Milestone (1), done (Jolt d4e7dfe2 on jolt/emitter-one-buffer, pushed; gates selfhost, corpus, errorreport, unit, stateimage, coreproc green): Parts, txt, join-txt and parts-text; 152 sites in emit, emit*, emit-invoke, emit-fn, emit-arity-clause, emit-loop, emit-try, sited-tail-call, ordered-call, with-once-clears and emit-numeric; text realized at the hoisted-constant pool (keyed and scanned by text) and the self-call placeholder rewrite. Output byte-identical: 543 stdlib forms (sha 8dd5292b) and the 400 src/seon forms (cmp equal). Emit allocation: stdlib 441.9 -> 381.9 MB (-13.6%); the 400 forms 1,159 -> 1,090 MB (-6%, 337 B a character). No real drop, so stopped before (2) and reported. The synthetic depth curve is unchanged (0.51, 1.24, 3.49, 11.16 MB at depth 50, 100, 200, 400): the superlinear growth is not the string copying but other per-level work in emit, not yet found; an allocation profile of emit by fn is the next measurement.

Profile (root's time-box, 2026-10-23; every jolt.* fn wrapped for calls and self bytes, Chez thread_bytes_allocated): on the 400 forms the top self allocation was chez-str-lit (string literals, docstrings above all) and char-escape: a one-character string per character joined by apply str over a lazy seq, about half of emit; munge-chars did the same for a name to escape. On the depth form every fn's call count is linear; the copy that stayed quadratic after milestone (1) was plain-call, still a str over its operands' parts. Fixed: Jolt 8a6bfc5b on jolt/emit-string-literals (from eba8826a, pushed), chez-str-lit and munge-chars in one indexed pass, with gate emitalloc (red before: 1,296 B a printable character, 1,656 escaped; green after: 256 and 340, ceilings 320 and 420). Alone, no new representation: the 400 forms 1,159 -> 593 MB (-49%), stdlib 441.9 -> 346.1 MB; the depth curve stays quadratic (10.6 MB at 400, 38.0 at 800). With Parts and plain-call on top (d7012c98 on jolt/emitter-one-buffer, pushed, not pinned): 539 MB (-53%), stdlib 278.7 MB, depth linear (3.1 MB at 400, 6.2 at 800). Output byte-identical in every variant. Self-review: chez-str-lit and munge-chars now take a string only; before, nil also passed (a symbol already threw, as Jolt cannot seq one). Every producer gives a string: fnsrc-name is reached only with a namespace (fnsrc-system-ns? is nil?), and the callers of chez-str-lit test sns/tns before calling. Jolt's gates and Seon's build and bin/prove on the pin hit no nil. Pinned 6e604ac8 (8a6bfc5b plus emitalloc asserting the emitted text, a past-BMP character included).

The proof at every milestone is byte-identical output: Jolt's selfhost (the minted seed byte for byte), corpus and errorreport gates. Plus a cost proof in bytes on nesting depth, red today (quadratic) and green linear. One Jolt pin bump at the end, through merge, with the cost proofs. Rejected: B, s-expressions handed to Chez (a bigger change: the AOT cache and the trace markers are text)."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/needs #{"jolt.backend/image-registration-is-opt-in"}
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.program-cost-test/a-defn-compiles-within-its-estimate}}
